 "findings": {
  "fit_budget": "Partly confirmed. With the Pivot settings linear learners move further after the flip (full learner's credibility weight 3.07 in A and 3.38 in B at 16-20 steps, against 3.67 and 3.61 with D1 settings; forgetting learner 1.96 and 2.24 against 3.16 and 3.02), and post-shift precision rises for every arm. But linear learners still sit at 4.1-4.5 before the shift against a true 3, and the larger budget makes MLPs more overconfident (pre-shift weight 8.0 in A and 14.3 in B against 4.4 and 7.5).",
  "ensembling": "Holds and grows. The single-donor table is below the four-donor table before the shift in all four groups, each interval excluding zero (-0.026 to -0.048). At matched evidence L0 against the single-donor table has every interval covering zero (8 of 8 cohort contrasts).",
  "forgetting": "Holds and widens. The forgetting learner raises post-shift precision in all four groups (+0.016 to +0.121, intervals excluding zero), now including linear learners, at a pre-shift cost of 0.010 to 0.051.",
  "untested": "Linear learners stay near the prior before the shift even with the larger budget. One candidate is selective labels: outcomes are seen only for shared items, with a 2% exploration floor. Not tested."
